From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 206/207] win32u: iOS: a process flushes only its own window
 surfaces

On iOS every Wine process is a pseudo-process of one app, so win32u's
list of window surfaces and its surfaces_lock are shared by all of
them, and flush_window_surfaces(), which a thread runs from its message
wait, flushed every process's surfaces instead of its own.

Borderlands 2's Steam prerequisites showed what that costs (PLA-870).
The VC++ 2005 ATL installer's inner process faulted in solid_rects_32
while painting its dialog, inside windrv_PatBlt, which holds the
surface's lock; the fault could not be dispatched, the process ended,
and the lock stayed held by a thread that no longer exists. The session
root's next message wait took surfaces_lock and waited on that lock for
ever, so the VC++ 2008 installer's dialog thread waited in
register_window_surface() as it showed "Extracting Files", its main
thread waited in a WM_SETTEXT sent to that dialog, and the app closed
the installer after 300 s: the Play failed. Desktop Wine and Proton
run the same installers in under a second each.

A process now skips a surface whose window is not its own
(is_current_process_window(), a read of the shared user handle table),
which is the set a desktop process's list holds. A surface an ended
process left behind is no longer touched.

The time a non-idle flush is throttled by (50 ms after going idle) was
a static, one value for every pseudo-process: once each process
flushed only its own surfaces, another process's idle flush would hold
back the flush of a process whose GUI thread paints but never goes
idle, and its windows would show nothing. Each thread now keeps the
time it last went idle (struct user_thread_info), which only ever
flushes more often than one time per process would.

Class: ios-port
Evidence: PLA-870 (the phone's log of IPA 0023f811: the session root in window_surface_flush on a lock whose owner thread is gone, the 2008 installer's thread in register_window_surface); tools/tests/test_window_surfaces_ios.py (this function, with an ended process's surface whose lock a dead thread holds: the caller's idle flush returns and flushes only its own surface; another process's idle flush, then the caller's non-idle one from a thread that never went idle: its surface is flushed)
Offered-upstream: no; iOS one-process runtime integration
---
 dlls/win32u/dce.c            | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 dlls/win32u/ntuser_private.h |  3 +++
 2 files changed, 27 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/dce.c b/dlls/win32u/dce.c
index 67d3dc8..2627c72 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/dce.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/dce.c
@@ -755,7 +755,16 @@ void register_window_surface( struct window_surface *old, struct window_surface
  */
 void flush_window_surfaces( BOOL idle )
 {
+#ifdef WINE_IOS
+    /* Playport (PLA-870): a static here is one time for every pseudo-process of the app,
+     * and a process flushes only its own surfaces below, so another process going idle
+     * held back the non-idle flush of a process whose thread never goes idle, and its
+     * windows showed nothing. Each thread keeps the time it last went idle. */
+    struct user_thread_info *thread_info = get_user_thread_info();
+    DWORD last_idle = thread_info->last_idle;
+#else
     static DWORD last_idle;
+#endif
     DWORD now;
     struct window_surface *surface;
 
@@ -766,9 +775,24 @@ void flush_window_surfaces( BOOL idle )
     else if ((int)(now - last_idle) < 50) goto done;
 
     LIST_FOR_EACH_ENTRY( surface, &window_surfaces, struct window_surface, entry )
+    {
+#ifdef WINE_IOS
+        /* Playport (PLA-870): every pseudo-process of the app shares this list, which on
+         * desktop holds only the calling process's surfaces. Flushing another process's
+         * surface waited on its lock, and a process that ended with a thread inside
+         * windrv_PatBlt left that lock held for ever: the session root's message wait
+         * stopped there holding surfaces_lock, and every window a later process showed
+         * waited in register_window_surface (Borderlands 2's VC++ 2008 prerequisite).
+         * A process flushes its own windows' surfaces, as on desktop. */
+        if (!is_current_process_window( surface->hwnd )) continue;
+#endif
         window_surface_flush( surface );
+    }
 done:
     pthread_mutex_unlock( &surfaces_lock );
+#ifdef WINE_IOS
+    thread_info->last_idle = last_idle;
+#endif
 }
 
 /***********************************************************************
diff --git a/dlls/win32u/ntuser_private.h b/dlls/win32u/ntuser_private.h
index 26bab84..954849c 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/ntuser_private.h
+++ b/dlls/win32u/ntuser_private.h
@@ -132,6 +132,9 @@ struct user_thread_info
     struct mouse_tracking_info   *mouse_tracking_info;    /* NtUserTrackMouseEvent handling */
     struct opengl_thread_data    *opengl_data;            /* OpenGL private thread data */
     struct list                   known_pointers;         /* list of known pointers */
+#ifdef WINE_IOS
+    DWORD                         last_idle;              /* flush_window_surfaces: when it last went idle */
+#endif
 };
 
 extern struct user_thread_info *get_user_thread_info(void);
